# Supabase / production DB safety

Live project `ksemrbndoenxdxijokke` holds real users, listings, packages, and coins.

## Never on production

- Run `supabase/migrations/20260801160000_init.sql` (or any full bootstrap) in the SQL Editor
- `DROP TABLE` / `TRUNCATE` on app tables (listings, profiles, subscriptions, payments, cities, …)
- `supabase db reset` or re-apply init against the live project
- “Fix schema by re-running init” — that wiped production twice

## Do instead

- Schema changes: **new additive** migration only  
  `supabase/migrations/YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.sql`
- Prefer `ALTER TABLE … ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS`, `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`
- Missing columns on live: use / extend `backend/scripts/repair-missing-schema.sql` (ALTERs only)
- Local throwaway DBs only for reset experiments; never the shared cloud project

## Before running any SQL against live

1. Skim for `DROP`, `TRUNCATE`, `DELETE FROM` without a tight `WHERE`
2. If unsure, stop and ask the user
3. Read `docs/db-safety.md`
